{"name":"Black Ice","hex":"#4d5051","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black ice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smooth, barely visible, and dangerously slippery film of ice, usually over a dark surface, such as rock or pavement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Ice (1992 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Ice is a 1992 Canadian–American thriller film directed by Neill Fearnley and starring Joanna Pacuła, Michael Ironside, Michael Nouri, Mickey Jones, Brent Neale, Harry Nelken, Arne Olsen, Gene Pyrz, Thom Schioler and Rick Skene. The film was shot on location in Winnipeg."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Ice_(1992_film)"},{"title":"Black Ice (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Ice is the fifteenth studio album by the Australian rock band AC/DC. First released in Europe on 17 October 2008 and released internationally on 20 October 2008, it was produced by Brendan O'Brien. It marked the band's first original recordings since Stiff Upper Lip (2000), with the eight-year gap being the longest between AC/DC's successive studio albums. The album was the band's final studio release to feature founding rhythm guitarist Malcolm Young, who left the band in September 2014 after being diagnosed with dementia, and died three years later."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Black_ice_red.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Ice_(album)"},{"title":"Black ice","blocks":[{"text":"Black ice, sometimes called clear ice, is a coating of glaze ice on a surface, for example on streets or on lakes. The ice itself is not black, but visually transparent, allowing the often black road below to be seen through it and light to be transmitted. The typically low levels of noticeable ice pellets, snow, or sleet surrounding black ice means that areas of the ice are often next to invisible to drivers, cyclists or people walking on it. Thus, there is a risk of slippage and subsequent accident due to the unexpected loss of traction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/2023-01-19_Pl%C3%B6tzliches_Glatteis_und_gefrorene_Pf%C3%BCtzen_in_Tauberbischofsheim.jpg/330px-2023-01-19_Pl%C3%B6tzliches_Glatteis_und_gefrorene_Pf%C3%BCtzen_in_Tauberbischofsheim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_ice"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Acdc_walmart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Acdc_walmart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Wal-Mart created special stands in their shops to promote AC/DC's Black Ice in North America.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAcdc_walmart.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Madrid-acdc_20.JPG/500px-Madrid-acdc_20.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Madrid-acdc_20.JPG/1280px-Madrid-acdc_20.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Madrid-acdc_20.JPG/500px-Madrid-acdc_20.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"AC/DC on-stage, Black Ice World Tour, Madrid, Spain, 5 June 2009","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadrid-acdc_20.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Panneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg/500px-Panneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Panneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg/1280px-Panneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Panneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg/500px-Panneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Warning sign for icy pavement in Quebec, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanneau_routier_Qu%C3%A9bec_gel_au_sol_-_Gasp%C3%A9.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Icyroadbridge.JPG/500px-Icyroadbridge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Icyroadbridge.JPG/1280px-Icyroadbridge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Icyroadbridge.JPG/500px-Icyroadbridge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Warning sign for bridge on US 